    <statement><p>Suppose the function <m>g</m> is given by the 
following table of values.</p>
<tabular bottom="medium" left="medium" right="medium" top="medium">
<row>
<cell> <m>y =</m> </cell>
<cell> -10 </cell>
<cell> -5 </cell>
<cell> 0 </cell>
<cell> 5 </cell>
<cell> 10 </cell>
</row>
<row>
<cell> <m>g(y) =</m> </cell>
<cell> 5 </cell>
<cell> -10 </cell>
<cell> -5 </cell>
<cell> 10 </cell>
<cell> 0 </cell>
</row>
</tabular>
<p>Use the table to fill in the missing values.
There may be more than one correct answer, in 
which case you should enter your answers as a 
comma separated list.  If there are no correct
answers, enter <em>NONE.</em></p>
<p><m>g(0)</m> = <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>g(10) =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>g \big(</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>\big) = 0</m></p>
<p><m>g \big(</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0004"/> <m>\big) = 10</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>10</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
